  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I need to find the rule that transforms input grids to output grids.\n\n**Observed Pattern:** For each row and column, I look for cells of the same color that belong to different 8-connected components. The gaps between such same-colored, different-component cells are filled with 5 in the output. All original colored cells become 0 (only the gaps become 5).\n\n**Rule:** \n1. Find 8-connected components of each color\n2. For each row/column, for each color appearing from \u22652 different components, fill the gap between adjacent different-component groups with 5\n3. Output is the union of all such fills\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    comp = {}\n    visited = set()\n    comp_id = 0\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and (r,c) not in visited:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                stack = [(r,c)]\n                visited.add((r,c))\n                while stack:\n                    cr, cc = stack.pop()\n                    comp[(cr,cc)] = comp_id\n                    for dr in [-1,0,1]:\n                        for dc in [-1,0,1]:\n                            if dr==0 and dc==0: continue\n                            nr, nc = cr+dr, cc+dc\n                            if 0<=nr<rows and 0<=nc<cols and (nr,nc) not in visited and grid[nr][nc]==color:\n                                visited.add((nr,nc))\n                                stack.append((nr,nc))\n                comp_id += 1\n    \n    output = [[0]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    def process_line(positions_and_comps):\n        comps = {}\n        for pos, cid in positions_and_comps:\n            if cid not in comps:\n                comps[cid] = []\n            comps[cid].append(pos)\n        if len(comps) < 2:\n            return []\n        sorted_comps = sorted(comps.items(), key=lambda x: min(x[1]))\n        fills = []\n        for i in range(len(sorted_comps)-1):\n            end1 = max(sorted_comps[i][1])\n            start2 = min(sorted_comps[i+1][1])\n            for p in range(end1+1, start2):\n                fills.append(p)\n        return fills\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        by_color = {}\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                if color not in by_color:\n                    by_color[color] = []\n                by_color[color].append((c, comp[(r,c)]))\n        for color, cells in by_color.items():\n            for c in process_line(cells):\n                output[r][c] = 5\n    \n    for c in range(cols):\n        by_color = {}\n        for r in range(rows):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                if color not in by_color:\n                    by_color[color] = []\n                by_color[color].append((r, comp[(r,c)]))\n        for color, cells in by_color.items():\n            for r in process_line(cells):\n                output[r][c] = 5\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    comp = {}\n    visited = set()\n    comp_id = 0\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0 and (r,c) not in visited:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                stack = [(r,c)]\n                visited.add((r,c))\n                while stack:\n                    cr, cc = stack.pop()\n                    comp[(cr,cc)] = comp_id\n                    for dr in [-1,0,1]:\n                        for dc in [-1,0,1]:\n                            if dr==0 and dc==0: continue\n                            nr, nc = cr+dr, cc+dc\n                            if 0<=nr<rows and 0<=nc<cols and (nr,nc) not in visited and grid[nr][nc]==color:\n                                visited.add((nr,nc))\n                                stack.append((nr,nc))\n                comp_id += 1\n    \n    output = [[0]*cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    def process_line(positions_and_comps):\n        comps = {}\n        for pos, cid in positions_and_comps:\n            if cid not in comps:\n                comps[cid] = []\n            comps[cid].append(pos)\n        if len(comps) < 2:\n            return []\n        sorted_comps = sorted(comps.items(), key=lambda x: min(x[1]))\n        fills = []\n        for i in range(len(sorted_comps)-1):\n            end1 = max(sorted_comps[i][1])\n            start2 = min(sorted_comps[i+1][1])\n            for p in range(end1+1, start2):\n                fills.append(p)\n        return fills\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        by_color = {}\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                if color not in by_color:\n                    by_color[color] = []\n                by_color[color].append((c, comp[(r,c)]))\n        for color, cells in by_color.items():\n            for c in process_line(cells):\n                output[r][c] = 5\n    \n    for c in range(cols):\n        by_color = {}\n        for r in range(rows):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                color = grid[r][c]\n                if color not in by_color:\n                    by_color[color] = []\n                by_color[color].append((r, comp[(r,c)]))\n        for color, cells in by_color.items():\n            for r in process_line(cells):\n                output[r][c] = 5\n    \n    return output",
